From 830fb5d0f5a4155134c3f8914019eebf791345da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:50:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RESEARCH-FLOOR-1: revise may not shrink a draft under the
 publish floor, complete extends a short draft to it (qnfo-research-exec
 0.21.0-floor)

Root cause: a complete draft under the 20,000-char publish floor (or under the reference floor) failed verify on gate-length /
gate-refcount, and the only tool for those gates was the find/replace patch reviser, which cannot add text; its strict retry even
asked the model to replace the offending sentence with an empty string. stageRevise also accepted any patch result of at least
10,000 chars, so a revise could take a 41k paper to 17k. The complete stage exited as soon as the paper was structurally complete.
Measured 2026-10-19: 113 of 255 complete events in 24 h under 20,000 chars, 21 gate-length / gate-refcount / HARD-unresolved
RESEARCH-TERMINAL issues in 24 h, 15 poison-parks in one day. The reviewer bibliography truncation (defect a) was already fixed in 0.19.0.

Change (qnfo-research-exec 0.19.6 -> 0.21.0, minor: new routes and a re-arm decision the worker takes on its own):
- REVISE-SHRINK-GUARD-1: a patch that takes a paper from at or above its floor to below it, cuts more than 20% of it in one pass
  (largest of 60 measured applied patches: 16%), or drops the cited references under the reference floor counts as not applied
  (event revise-shrink-refused); the second-model path runs with the length floor and the allowed removal stated in the per-call
  text (cached prefix unchanged). ops_config research_revise_shrink_guard = measure restores the old behaviour.
- COMPLETE-TO-FLOOR-1: stageComplete extends a complete paper under the floor with one grounded section per round (new EXTEND task,
  inserted before the Discussion, cites the uncited bibliography entries, at most 6 rounds, stall rule, goal 1.2x the floor because a
  single patch shrinks up to 16%). stageVerify routes a first-pass gate-length / gate-refcount-only failure to complete with
  verifyPass 1 (the second verify stays terminal); stageRevise routes floor-only fixes to complete without a patch call, and a patched
  paper still short is extended before review. ops_config research_floor_extend = off restores the old exit.
- FLOOR-REARM-1: the migration cannot re-queue anything (it runs at merge, before the deploy is live); it freezes the 31 candidates
  in bak_20261019_research_parked and the corrected worker's hourly floorRearmTick returns 5 per run to complete, once each. A missing
  backup table or park_rearm = off makes it a no-op.
- Migration migrations/2026-10-19-research-rearm-after-repair.sql: the backup, control_registry rows (gate, guard, cap), failure_modes
  research-draft-below-floor and research-revise-shrink with fm-<key> detector contracts, the closing probe of issue 99913 (its own was a
  vacuous closure check) as a separate UPDATE plus a separate activation, and the decision_log row.

Tests: qnfo-research-exec/revise-shrink-guard.test.mjs (28 checks) and complete-to-floor.test.mjs (59 checks, incl. the migration, the
detectors and the 99913 probe on node:sqlite) run the real stageRevise, stageComplete, stageVerify, floorRearmTick and the migration.
Against the base worker.js (with stubs for the functions it lacks) they fail 6 + crash and 26; with the change 28/28 and 59/59.

Issues: QNFO/qnfo-workers (D1 agent_issues 99913, 99943, 100024, 100026; GitHub #2800 closed by 0.19.0); clusters
research-pipeline-1/research-short-drafts-blind-reviewer-terminal-parks and research-pipeline-2/research-terminal-length-floor.

